# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Artwork you do not have the right to redistribute goes in asset/local/.
#
# The rule this file is really enforcing: a repository should contain exactly
# the pixels it is allowed to publish, and nothing else. asset/ is for artwork
# that may be redistributed; asset/local/ is for the rest -- the clip you are
# developing against, a client's logo, a purchase you cannot share.
#
# It is a convenience, not a guarantee. tools/embed-asset.mjs copies artwork
# into client.js, and there is no .gitignore pattern that can hide a copy living
# inside a tracked file. That is why inlining from asset/local/ prints a warning
# and why `--clear` exists:
#
#     node tools/embed-asset.mjs --clear
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
asset/local/

# Generated pages. Both carry a copy of the artwork -- preview.html embeds the
# same inlined payload, preview.png is that artwork rendered -- so committing
# them would mean committing the pixels twice more, in two more places that
# would each have to be re-checked when the artwork changes.
#
#     node tools/build-preview.mjs
preview.html
preview.png

# Scratch from tools/verify-chromium.mjs. Removed on exit, but a killed run
# leaves them behind and they should never reach the index.
.verify-profile/
.verify-blank.html

# Written by tools/check-embed.mjs, which restores client.js in a finally block.
# Only present if that run was interrupted.
client.js.check-embed-backup

# Raw frame dumps from the asset pipelines: the `.frames-*.raw` temp file that
# tools/build-*.sh create, and frames.raw from the README recipe.
.frames-*.raw
frames.raw

# Screenshots from experimenting.
shot*.png

node_modules/

#And...
MAINTAINING.md
